   "note": "Trusted local host boundary (internal/auth + internal/host) with the OS-scoped named-pipe NativeBridge: one-time OWNER bootstrap bound to the current Windows SID with duplicate-bootstrap and multi-owner refusal, short session renewal that revokes exactly the credential it supersedes, DPAPI-protected provider-credential vault reachable only through the bridge, workspace-root binding pinned by volume serial + file index with per-access reparse/permission checks, and single-use five-minute selection references. Binding: test.security -> go run ./tests/security/check, 148 unique assertions, 4 clean runs, dispatcher invocation eaed2c8d. Accepted only after a REJECT: round 1 (w1701_verifier) found the serve-path peer gate unasserted, reply grading decorative, a raw-ASCII-only leak scan, a self-fulfilling read-only-root assertion, a client-named workspace hole and lingering superseded tokens; each was fixed in product code and is now caught by a named assertion plus a mutation (see mutation_selfcheck.json, 11 mutations, every one caught). Round 2 (w1701_verifier_r2) returned ACCEPT_WITH_RESERVATIONS; the reservations were answered in post_review_addendum.json - two were fixed with new assertions (transport refusal must not echo material; the chooser's directory wins over a client hint) and the rest are disclosed as open. Disclosed open: import/choose withdrawal closures are not exercised (no reachable nonconformant input), proving the DEFAULT peer lookup needs a second interactive OS account (W17-99 resource), per-directory single-owner-instance locking, loopback first-connect flakiness on this machine (mitigated by harness warm-up, disclosed not eliminated), and three gofmt-dirty files outside this card's write_scope. apps/cli and apps/control are NOT yet rewired onto this host. Construction check only - parent W17, its formal cases A10/A11/C02/C22 and the W17 gates remain open. No completion claim: 22 parent tasks and 42 formal cases are required."
  },
